                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A beautiful indie gem, totally psychedelic and humoristic alien octopus platformer / exploration game. What I liked the most were the colors, design and visual effects which are a total success. Also the music soundtrack is remarkable, especially in some places (like on the last level in which it sounds like Vangelis). You can beat the game in 4h, and there is a lot of replay value if you want to find all secrets and hidden portals. The only downside are the controls (lack of inertia and sluggish movements, and also awkward controller configuration (I made a Community Controller Configuration that makes the game more enjoyable with a xbox controller). This is not a big problem for the first 80% of the game, but the last levels are a bit a pain in the neck because of this. To conclude, I would say that the game is not perfect and feels unpolished on some aspects (surely because of the use of a third party game maker engine), but there is a great quality in aesthetics, music and level design which deserves your attention if you like this kind. 7/10",
                        "timestamp_created": 1513439838,
